        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cf76a283-0ac3-52ca-b3ca-3a358249db9d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Phil Hellmuth, Johnny Chan, Stu Ungar\n- Events: 1989 World Series of Poker Main Event, 1980 World Series of Poker Main Event\n- Topics: WSOP Main Event youngest winner record, World Series of Poker bracelets\n\nFacts:\n- In 1980, Stu Ungar set the record as the youngest winner of the World Series of Poker Main Event.\n- Phil Hellmuth was born on July 16, 1964.\n- In 1989, 24-year-old Phil Hellmuth won the World Series of Poker Main Event by defeating defending champion Johnny Chan.\n- In 1989, Phil Hellmuth broke Stu Ungar's record to become the youngest player to win the World Series of Poker Main Event.\n- Phil Hellmuth is an American professional poker player.\n- Phil Hellmuth has won a record fourteen World Series of Poker bracelets.",
